    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 1
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "About page"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "0a9f21cb",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 2
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Design"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "c9d931c2",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "A single static "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "About",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " page on the public site: one heading and a few body paragraphs served at "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " to every visitor, plus a navigation link to it from the landing page. No editing, no personalisation, no localisation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "2a9679a1",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Reuse check (live catalogs):",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "platformEntities",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " lists 60 served entities — all demo ("
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "simpledao.*",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "), platform-internal ("
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "system.*",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ") or knowledge/registry entities; none models public page content, and the spec's Data model section explicitly says none is created. The repository is a bare Maven jar ("
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "com.example:projecytt",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ", Java 23, "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "zero dependencies",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " per "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "pom.xml",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ") whose only source is "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "src/main/java/com/example/App.java",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (a Hello-World main that prints to stdout). There is no web layer, no landing page, no stylesheet and no navigation markup — this feature introduces all of them, and the tasks below say so rather than instructing an agent to reuse artifacts that do not exist. "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "platformSpecs",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " shows only "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "spec1 v2",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " registered — this feature's own spec — so no other spec's ground is overlapped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "675682f7",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Serving mechanism (established by this feature):",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " the project has no framework and the spec adds none, so the design uses the JDK's built-in "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ", started from the existing "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "App.main",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ", with no new Maven dependency. The server binds "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "port 8080 by default",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ", overridable via the "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "APP_PORT",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " environment variable (documented default 8080), so the HTTP checks in Tasks 2–3 are deterministic. A small shared page-shell (layout chrome + stylesheet, with an empty navigation region) is created by Task 1; Task 2 registers the "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " route through it, and Task 3 populates the shell's navigation region with the site's nav markup. Because every page renders through the same shell, the nav appears on both the landing page and "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " without duplication."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "6aad3046",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Data model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "982ffd2b",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "None. The spec fixes this: "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "\"the page content is static; no entities are created or stored.\"",
      "styles" : {
        "italic" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " The heading and body paragraphs are constants in the page artifact itself — no entity, no persistence, no migration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "30d08ac3",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Page content"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "3be33a4d",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Route:",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ", reachable without authentication (spec Constraint: readable by unauthenticated visitors). The server binds port 8080 (or "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "APP_PORT",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " if set) and registers no auth handler, so any HTTP client can fetch the page."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "d568afb7",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Heading:",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " \"About\" — the text A1 asserts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "229cccb3",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Body:",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " a short description of who the company is and what it does — a few paragraphs of fixed prose, no interactive elements beyond the site's standard navigation (spec User interface)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "257c6b24",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Styling:",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " consistent with the rest of the site because every page renders through the same shared shell. "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "This feature establishes that shell",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (layout chrome + stylesheet) — it is not inherited from a landing page that does not yet exist; the About page adds its own content region inside the shell Task 1 creates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "edcb28a7",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Navigation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "fc1a1a1e",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "The site's main navigation carries one link labelled \"About\" pointing at "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (A2). The shell created in Task 1 reserves an empty navigation region; Task 3 populates that region with the nav markup (including the About link). Since both the landing page and "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " render through the same shell, the populated nav renders on both without any per-visitor state and without duplicated markup."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "ddd55fc6",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "View layouts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "93115726",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "None — this feature serves fixed prose, not a data-backed view. There is no entity to lay out, no ViewType applies, and the spec's UI section asks only for a heading plus paragraphs in the site's chrome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "369f4017",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 2
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Tasks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "0a47bd5a",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Task 1: Establish the web layer — HTTP server, shared page shell and stylesheet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "1d89b272",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Extend the existing "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "src/main/java/com/example/App.java",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (currently a Hello-World main) to start an embedded HTTP server using the JDK's built-in "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " — no new Maven dependency in "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "pom.xml",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ". The server binds port "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "8080 by default",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ", overridable via the "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "APP_PORT",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " environment variable (default 8080 when unset). Create the site's shared page shell: a layout template (HTML chrome: "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "<head>",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ", stylesheet link, an "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "empty",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " navigation region, content region) and a small stylesheet, in a new source location such as "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "src/main/resources/web/",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ". The shell is minimal but shared — every page this feature introduces renders through it, which is what keeps the About page consistent with the rest of the site. The shell's nav region is left empty here; Task 3 fills it. The server must serve pages to unauthenticated visitors (no auth handler registered)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "c12ed0c2",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Acceptance criteria",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ":"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "5546d82b",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Starting "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "App.main",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " binds the HTTP server to port 8080 (or "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "APP_PORT",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " when set), and a request to an unregistered path (e.g. "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ") returns a well-formed 404 rendered through the shared shell — this verifies the server and shell run, with no dependency on Tasks 2–3."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "7cfa4c54",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "No new Maven dependency is added."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "1eaa236b",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Task 2: Create the static /about page"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "2583e9a5",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Register the "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " route on the HTTP server from Task 1. The page renders through the shared shell from Task 1: an "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "<h1>",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " with the text \"About\" followed by a few fixed body paragraphs describing who the company is and what it does, in the shell's content region. The content is a constant in the page artifact — do NOT introduce an entity, a content store, a CMS hook or an editing path; the spec's Data model section rules that out explicitly. Depends on Task 1 (server and shell must exist first)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "9160fd97",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Acceptance criteria",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ":"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "36a003c4",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "(A1) WHEN "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " is opened — i.e. starting the app and requesting "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "http://localhost:8080/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " over HTTP — the page displays the \"About\" heading and its body paragraphs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "2bfc43c9",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Requesting "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " over plain HTTP with no credentials, cookies or auth headers returns 200 with the full page content (spec Constraint: readable by unauthenticated visitors)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "c5443d72",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Task 3: Create the landing page and populate the shared navigation with the About link"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "8a66f7f6",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Create the landing page (the site's "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " route) rendering through the same shared shell from Task 1, and populate the shell's empty navigation region with the site's main navigation markup: a link labelled \"About\" whose target is "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ". Because both pages render through the same shell, this one nav region serves the landing page and "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " alike — do not duplicate nav markup per page. This task "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "creates",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " the landing page and the nav markup — neither exists in the repository today; it does not modify an existing page. Do NOT add any other landing-page section (out of scope per the spec). Depends on Task 2: the link's target route must exist first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "739880a9",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Acceptance criteria",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ":"
    } ]
  }, {
